cells:
  - kind: 1
    value: |
      # Greeting and NL2SQL workers for the existing tree team

      This notebook adds TREE_GREETING_AGENT and TREE_NL2SQL_AGENT to the
      existing TREE_DENSITY_MAP_TEAM. It keeps the density, discovery, SVM,
      and K-means workers. 

      The greeting is a fixed, reviewed introduction to the two original
      translated datasets. NL2SQL uses its own profile, restricted to the
      tree-project tables and views that currently exist. TREE_SQL_CONTEXT_TOOL
      refreshes that profile's object list before each SQL question, so a
      result created later by an OML worker is available on the next request.
      Context/profile changes do not modify dataset rows.

      Run definition cells top to bottom after the four existing tree workers
      are installed. Run the final team cell only when no team request is in
      progress. Tests are in 4-bomen_OML_greeting_NL2SQL_tests.sqlnb.
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 1
    value: |
      ## 1. Fixed greeting content

      The function returns the exact original table names, 26 tree columns,
      eight neighbourhood columns, and example questions with table/view and
      column names. It does not inspect the schema at greeting time or report
      invented row counts.
    languageId: markdown
  - kind: 2
    value: |-
