      --         {"question":"How are Quercus robur trees grouped by age and diameter class?","tables_or_views":["TREE_KMEANS_RESULTS_V"],"columns":["RUN_ID","SOURCE_RECORD_ID","TREE_AGE","TRUNK_DIAMETER","CLUSTER_ID"]},
      --         {"question":"Which SVM-flagged trees are in each K-means group?","tables_or_views":["TREE_ANOMALY_RESULTS_V","TREE_KMEANS_RESULTS_V"],"columns":["RUN_ID","SOURCE_RECORD_ID","ANOMALY_FLAG","CLUSTER_ID"]}
      --       ],
      --       "note":"These are examples, not a complete question list. SQL can answer broader questions over approved objects that exist. Ask the supervisor to run density, SVM, or K-means for a new analysis. Saved result views omit geometry; spatial tables or saved GeoJSON support maps. A model flag is a record for review, not a health diagnosis."
